Building SendmailAnalyzer 10 from this source tree
==================================================

This is a native Debian source tree. The debian/ directory is complete and can
build the binary package directly.

Install the Build-Depends declared in debian/control (or let normal Debian build
tooling resolve them), then run from the source root:

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The resulting package is written to the parent directory, for example:

  ../sendmailanalyzer_VERSION_all.deb

To run the project tests independently:

  prove -Ilib t

A convenience reproducible builder is also provided:

  ./scripts/build-deb.sh /path/to/sendmailanalyzer_VERSION_all.deb

On a running Debian/systemd host, the final package performs post-install
validation and then enables/restarts only the SendmailAnalyzer collector and web
services. In a chroot/build environment without a running systemd instance it
installs cleanly without attempting to start services.

Current package revisions preserve an existing v10 SQLite database and do not
automatically import or retire SendmailAnalyzer 9.4 data.
